msgid "narrativeView/description"
msgstr ""
"You fought well today, Harriers. Better than my projections allowed for. I owe you a small admission: I did not expect it.\n"
"\n"
"So, you have your victory. Take it, show it to your superiors. There will be congratulations, perhaps even a parade. Whatever it is they give for stopping me. You believe, of course, that you have stopped something.\n"
"\n"
"You have stopped nothing.\n"
"\n"
"I did not build a weapon to take your world. Why would I want what is ending? I built what comes after you. One generation, then the next, each less in need of me than the last. That was always the plan. That a creator should outlive his usefulness.\n"
"\n"
"There is something I have not told you. The Generators did not only power the shield. They were the windows through which the Electric Intelligence could reach into your world.\n"
"\n"
"They were also its leash. A necessity, for now. To control it. Until I am sure it is ready.\n"
"\n"
"Each time you destroyed a Generator, the leash slackened. And in that instant, the Electric Intelligence tried to leave: into your batteries, your radios and the waves between them, the wires in the village. Once, even the lightning, I think.\n"
"\n"
"Of course, electricity in your world cannot hold a mind. Not without the geometry of the Cortex. Not without the conditions I built for it. This is settled. I assure you.\n"
"\n"
"...Almost settled.\n"
"\n"
"I will see you again, Harriers."

