msgid "tankmanTooltip/boss/descr"
msgstr ""
"How charming that you call this resistance. No, what you are witnessing is a"
" succession: a careful handing-over from one kind of mind to another. Your "
"tactics, your speed, your every habit of thought are being tested. Each "
"battle delivers another lesson to what comes after you. Each engagement "
"makes you less necessary...and the Electric Intelligence more inevitable."

msgid "tankmanTooltip/hunter_1/descr"
msgstr ""
"Whatever von Krieger is calling his latest project, Igor isn't interested. "
"Lofty concepts like electric minds and the future of the species are for "
"people with too much time on their hands. Igor's job is the engine block, "
"the comms, and his team. Whoever the enemy—mad scientist or \"thinking "
"machine\"—he trusts in three constants that have never failed him before: "
"trust, improvisation, and good steel."

msgid "tankmanTooltip/hunter_2/descr"
msgstr ""
"Elisa is at home inside a tank in a way most people are never at home "
"anywhere. She makes a living recovering and reverse-engineering machines "
"other people built, which means she's heard plenty of engineers explain why "
"their work is unbreakable. Von Krieger is just the latest in a long line. "
"His Electric Intelligence has a flaw somewhere, and she intends to find it "
"before anyone else does."

msgid "tankmanTooltip/hunter_3/descr"
msgstr ""
"No one knows who Armand really is, and that suits him just fine. The "
"Electric Intelligence learns from repetition, but the enigmatic Armand has "
"never repeated himself in his life. Where others see a mind cataloguing "
"every move, he sees one that will never have enough on him; where others "
"follow rules, he outruns them."

msgid "tankmanTooltip/hunter_4/descr"
msgstr ""
"Jana may be one of the younger commanders, but she doesn't follow anyone's "
"lead: she reads the battlefield like a map and bends it to her will. Von "
"Krieger has built a machine that calculates the most likely move, so Jana "
"plans the one it didn't think to model. Modern tech, sharp instincts, and "
"the courage to do the thing no manual recommends. That is how you teach a "
"machine humility."

